abstract: >-
  DATect is a one-week-ahead quantitative forecasting system for domoic acid (DA)
  contamination of shellfish at 10 monitoring sites along the U.S. Pacific Northwest
  coast. It combines an XGBoost + Random Forest ensemble with per-site hyperparameter
  customization, observation-order lag features for sparse/irregular DA measurements,
  and a dedicated transition-focused binary classifier for early-warning alerts.
  The system enforces leak-free retrospective validation throughout and reports
  honest multi-seed bootstrap confidence intervals on a chronological 2022-2023
  holdout window that was never inspected during configuration selection.
